---
import FaqLanding from '../../components/FaqLanding.astro';

const faqs = [
	{
		q: 'We are registered with the SEC. Do we also have NPC obligations?',
		a: '<strong>Yes. The SEC licenses you; the NPC regulates your borrower data.</strong> The SEC covers your licence, disclosures and interest practices. The National Privacy Commission (NPC) separately regulates how you handle borrower personal data under RA 10173, with a lending-specific rulebook (NPC Circular 20-01, as amended by Circular 2022-02). The two regulators act together: SEC Memorandum Circular 18-2019 ties your licence to lawful collection practices, and a 2025 joint DICT-NPC-SEC advisory targets online lending platforms.',
	},
	{
		q: 'Why are lending apps under so much scrutiny?',
		a: '<strong>Because contact-list harvesting and borrower shaming are the NPC’s most active enforcement docket.</strong> The NPC has shut down online lending companies, ordered app takedowns, and referred executives for prosecution over apps that harvest phone contacts, photos and location to pressure borrowers. If you operate or use a lending app, how it accesses the phone is the first thing a regulator inspects.',
	},
	{
		q: 'What borrower data counts as sensitive, and why does it matter?',
		a: '<strong>Government IDs are sensitive personal information by law, and the rest of the borrower file rides with them.</strong> Payslips, bank details and income documents are the data that enables identity fraud, so a leak of them is a reportable breach. Sensitive data triggers the strictest duties: a lawful basis, consent done properly, security measures and retention limits. Setting these up is the DPO’s job.',
	},
	{
		q: 'Does a lending company need a Data Protection Officer?',
		a: '<strong>Yes, whatever your size.</strong> Every organization that processes personal data must designate a DPO (IRR Section 26(a)). What is specific to lending comes next: credit scoring is profiling, so your data processing systems must be registered with the NPC at any size (NPC Circular 2022-04, Section 5), and a borrower file with the government IDs of 1,000 or more people triggers registration on its own. The DPO is your registered contact with the NPC.',
	},
	{
		q: 'What about collections and debt-shaming complaints?',
		a: '<strong>Collection is where most lending complaints start.</strong> Contacting a borrower’s relatives or co-workers, or disclosing their debt, is unlawful processing under the DPA and an unfair collection practice under SEC rules. Circular 20-01 limits character references to the names the borrower supplied and keeps you liable for outsourced collectors. A privacy-compliant collection script protects you from both NPC fines and SEC sanctions.',
	},
	{
		q: 'How fast must we report a data breach?',
		a: '<strong>Within 72 hours of knowing about it.</strong> If borrower data that could enable fraud may have been taken, you must notify the NPC and the affected borrowers within 72 hours and file a full report within five days (NPC Circular 16-03). We prepare the response plan in advance so you are not improvising against the clock.',
	},
	{
		q: 'What can this cost us if we get it wrong?',
		a: '<strong>Fines, licence sanctions and personal criminal exposure, all at once.</strong> NPC administrative fines reach 0.5% to 3% of prior-year gross income for a grave infraction, capped at ₱5 million per act, plus ₱50,000 to ₱200,000 per infraction for failing to register. The SEC can suspend or revoke your licence for the same conduct. Lending executives have faced criminal referral with prison terms of up to seven years for unlawful processing. NPC fine decisions are immediately executory even while you appeal.',
	},
	{
		q: 'Can you act as our external DPO and fix this end to end?',
		a: '<strong>Yes.</strong> As a TÜV Certified DPO (Cert #7000532) in Region 8, I can serve as your designated DPO, handle NPC registration, build your Privacy Management Program, review your app and collection practices, and train your staff and collectors.',
	},
];
---

<FaqLanding
	title="Data Privacy Compliance for Lending & Financing Companies | TÜV Certified DPO"
	description="SEC and NPC duties, borrower PII, lending-app scrutiny, and DPO requirements for lending and financing companies in Region 8, Philippines."
	badge="For Lending & Financing"
	heading="Data privacy compliance for lending companies"
	intro={[
		"You scanned this from our Lending Risk Summary. Lending and financing companies answer to both the SEC and the NPC, and lending apps draw the closest scrutiny of any sector. Here is what that means in plain terms.",
	]}
	faqs={faqs}
	ctaHeading="Lend with borrower data handled lawfully"
/>
